        <div style="flex:1 1 400px;min-width:300px;">
          <div style={eyebrow}>quickstart</div>
          <h2 style={h2Style + "font-size:clamp(30px,3.6vw,46px);"}>Five minutes from clone to your first item.</h2>
          <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#A6A1C2;margin:0 0 16px;max-width:520px;">Sign up the first user. They get <span style="font-family:'JetBrains Mono',monospace;color:#b9a3ff;">admin</span>. From there, define a collection in the admin and the API endpoint exists immediately — no redeploy, no codegen step, no schema versioning gymnastics.</p>
          <p style="font-size:16px;line-height:1.65;color:#A6A1C2;margin:0 0 26px;max-width:520px;">Drop a column, the column is gone. Rename a collection, the API path moves with it.</p>
